{% extends "admin/layout.twig" %}
{% block topbar_title %}Judging schedule{% endblock %}
{% block topbar_actions %}<a class="ad-btn" href="/admin/judges">All judges</a>{% endblock %}

{#
  ── THE ROUND, IN ONE PLACE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Every other screen that reads a sitting reads ONE of them. So an operator running
  a panel of ten across forty entries had the whole round in the database and no way
  to answer "what is Tuesday", "does Dr Achebe know about Thursday", or "did the
  calendar actually take it".

  Three things this screen is careful about:

    · The Google check is a BUTTON. Forty sittings is forty round trips to an Apps
      Script deployment, and a screen that spends the script's quota every time
      somebody glances at it stops working during the round it exists for.

    · A sitting with no meeting link is called out rather than left blank. A blank
      cell reads as a rendering fault; "no link yet" is a job.

    · The reminder is sent by a person pressing a button, and the button says how
      many people it reaches before it is pressed. There is no undo on an email.
#}

{% block content %}

{# ── CAN THE GOOGLE SIDE BE ASKED AT ALL? ────────────────────────────────────
   Said once, at the top, rather than as forty identical failures further down.
   Every part of this integration can be configured correctly and still do nothing,
   and from the .env file the five ways it fails look identical. #}
{% if not meet %}
<div class="ad-card" style="margin-bottom:16px;border-left:4px solid var(--ad-gold,#c79a3a)">
  <div class="ad-card__body">
    <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px"><strong>The calendar cannot be checked from here.</strong>
      {{ meet_why }}</p>
    <p style="margin:7px 0 0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">
      The schedule below is still what this platform holds — it just cannot be compared
      against Google until the Apps Script side answers. The reminders do not need it.</p>
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

{# ── WHO TO REMIND ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   First, because it is why somebody opened this screen mid-round.

   Three scopes, and each button states its own blast radius. "Remind everyone" on a
   panel of ten is ten emails and there is no undo, so the count is on the button
   rather than in a confirmation nobody reads. #}
<div class="ad-card" style="margin-bottom:16px">
  <div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">Send a reminder<small>
    Each judge gets their own sittings, the joining links, and one calendar file that
    adds all of them at once.</small></div></div>
  <div class="ad-card__body">

    {% if judges is empty %}
      {# Not an error state and not an empty table: nothing is scheduled, which is a
         different fact and has a different next step. #}
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
        Nobody has a sitting in the next few days, so there is nothing to remind anybody
        about. Schedule the interviews first —
        <a href="/admin/interviews">the interview queue</a> is where that happens.</p>
    {% else %}

      {% if programmes|length > 1 %}
      {# `.ad-form` styles its own labels and controls by descendant selector — there is
         no `ad-label` or `ad-input` class in the admin sheet, and inventing one produces
         an unstyled field that looks deliberate. `AdminClassCoverageTest` exists because
         two forms once wrote `ad-form__row`, which was never a selector either. #}
      <form method="get" action="/admin/judges/schedule" class="ad-form" style="margin:0 0 14px">
        <div style="max-width:22rem">
          <label for="jsProg">Programme</label>
          <select id="jsProg" name="programme">
            <option value="">Every programme</option>
            {% for p in programmes %}
              <option value="{{ p.id }}"{{ programme == p.id ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ p.title }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
          </select>
        </div>
        <button class="ad-btn" type="submit" style="margin-top:9px">Show</button>
      </form>
      {% endif %}

      <div style="display:flex;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center">
        {# `data-confirm` routes the submit through agConfirm — the admin CSP has no
           'unsafe-inline', so there is no onsubmit here and there must not be. #}
        <form method="post" action="/admin/judges/schedule/remind"
              data-confirm="Send every judge their schedule and joining links now? This reaches {{ judges|length }} inbox{{ judges|length == 1 ? '' : 'es' }} immediately and an email cannot be unsent.">
          <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
          <input type="hidden" name="scope" value="all">
          <button class="ad-btn ad-btn--primary" type="submit">
            Remind all {{ judges|length }} judge{{ judges|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</button>
        </form>

        {% if programme %}
        <form method="post" action="/admin/judges/schedule/remind"
              data-confirm="Send this programme's panel their sittings for it? Judges on other programmes hear nothing, and an email cannot be unsent.">
          <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
          <input type="hidden" name="scope" value="programme">
          <input type="hidden" name="programme" value="{{ programme }}">
          <button class="ad-btn" type="submit">Remind this programme only</button>
        </form>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      <p style="margin:11px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">
        A judge with nothing scheduled is never mailed, even by “remind all” — a reminder
        about no meetings is the fastest way to teach a panel to ignore us.
      </p>

      {# ── AND ONE AT A TIME ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
         The commonest real request is "she says she never got it", which is one
         person and not a broadcast. #}
      <div class="ad-table-wrap" style="margin-top:14px">
        <table class="ad-table">
          <thead><tr>
            <th scope="col">Judge</th><th scope="col">Sittings</th>
            <th scope="col">Next</th><th scope="col"></th>
          </tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for j in judges %}
            <tr>
              <td><strong style="font-size:13px">{{ j.name }}</strong>
                <div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">{{ j.email }}</div></td>
              <td style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace">{{ j.sittings }}</td>
              <td style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;white-space:nowrap">
                {{ j.next ? j.next|when_zoned('D j M, H:i') : '—' }}</td>
              <td>
                <form method="post" action="/admin/judges/schedule/remind"
                      data-confirm="Send this judge their sittings and joining links now? Nobody else is written to, and an email cannot be unsent. ({{ j.name }} — {{ j.sittings }} sitting{{ j.sittings == 1 ? '' : 's' }}.)">
                  <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="scope" value="judge">
                  <input type="hidden" name="judge_id" value="{{ j.id }}">
                  <button class="ad-btn" type="submit" style="min-height:34px;padding:0 12px">Remind</button>
                </form>
              </td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>

{# ── THE CALENDAR ITSELF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Grouped by day, which is how an operator thinks about a round. The day heading
   is computed in PHP: a template that derives it per row gets the boundary wrong
   at midnight in the display zone. #}
{% if by_day is empty %}
<div class="ad-card"><div class="ad-card__body">
  <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px">Nothing is scheduled in the window
    (from three days ago onward). Sittings appear here as soon as they have a date —
    see <a href="/admin/interviews">the interview queue</a>.</p>
</div></div>
{% else %}
{% for day, rows in by_day %}
<div class="ad-card" style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">
    {{ day|when('l j F Y') }}<small>{{ rows|length }} sitting{{ rows|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</small>
  </div></div>
  <div class="ad-table-wrap">
    <table class="ad-table">
      <thead><tr>
        <th scope="col">Time</th><th scope="col">Nominee</th>
        <th scope="col">Panel</th><th scope="col">Meeting</th>
        <th scope="col">Calendar</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for s in rows %}
        <tr>
          <td style="font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;white-space:nowrap">
            {{ s.when|when('H:i') }} {{ tz_abbr() }}
            <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">{{ s.minutes }} min</div></td>
          <td>
            <a href="{{ s.admin_url }}" style="font-weight:600;font-size:13px">{{ s.nominee }}</a>
            {% if s.category %}<div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">{{ s.category }}</div>{% endif %}
          </td>
          <td>
            {% if s.panel is empty %}
              {# Named rather than blank. A sitting with no panel is a room with a nominee
                 in it and nobody to judge them, and it is silent until the day. #}
              <span class="ad-chip ad-chip--red">No panel yet</span>
            {% else %}
              <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px">
                {% for j in s.panel %}<span class="ad-chip ad-chip--grey">{{ j.name }}</span>{% endfor %}
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
          <td>
            {% if s.meet_url %}
              <a href="{{ s.meet_url }}" rel="noopener" style="font-size:12px">Join link</a>
            {% else %}
              <span class="ad-chip ad-chip--gold">No link yet</span>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
          <td>
            {% if not s.has_event %}
              <span class="ad-chip ad-chip--gold">Never synced</span>
            {% elseif meet %}
              {# On demand, per sitting. The answer is a fact about right now, so it is
                 flashed rather than stored — a stored verdict is stale the moment
                 somebody drags the event in Google, which is the case this catches. #}
              <form method="post" action="/admin/judges/schedule/{{ s.id }}/verify">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
                <button class="ad-btn" type="submit" style="min-height:32px;padding:0 11px;font-size:12px">
                  Check Google</button>
              </form>
            {% else %}
              {# NOT "Synced". All we know is that an event id was stored when the sitting
                 was created; whether Google still holds it is exactly what we cannot ask
                 right now. Claiming the stronger thing here would be the same fault as a
                 status page reporting health it has not checked. #}
              <span class="ad-chip ad-chip--grey"
                    title="An event was created for this sitting. It cannot be verified until the Apps Script side answers.">Event on file</span>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<div class="ad-card"><div class="ad-card__body">
  <p style="margin:0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
    <strong>“Check Google” answers three different things.</strong> That the calendar agrees;
    that it holds the sitting at a <em>different</em> time, which means somebody moved it
    there and every invitation we have already sent carries ours; or that the event is gone.
    A fourth answer — that the script could not be reached — is reported as itself and never
    as “missing”, because recreating forty events that already exist is the expensive mistake.
  </p>
</div></div>

{% endblock %}
